# Network play between two machines (docs/phase-network.md, stage N6), the joiner's side of net_host.kps: the join
# screen lists the host's game as the local network's broadcast finds it, or as --lan-host NAME[:PORT] asks it (a host
# on another --lan-port, so no broadcast reaches it), and Ok joins it. In the game the joiner moves a worker and logs the
# shared hash at tick 400, which must equal the host's. Played between a desktop and a phone (Android: the debug
# bundle's generated/scripts/net_lan_join.kps), not by tools/ci.sh: one machine's two programs are net_join.kps's.
options originals
clock real
wait screen gluMain
click control gluMain.4
wait dialog gluGameMode and still
click control glugamemode.original
wait screen gluConn
click control gluConn.9
wait dialog gluPEdit and still
text "Join"
click control gluPEdit.1
wait screen gluLogin
click control glulogin.ok
wait screen gluJoin
wait list.count >= 1 within 120000
until dialog gluChat every 2 click control gluJoin.13
# the host's Start waits up to 300 s for the map to reach this program (net_host.kps), then the countdown
wait game within 360000
log started tick units:0 units:1
wait tick >= 40
select worker 96
expect selected > 0
rclick center -160 96
wait tick >= 400 within 120000
log played tick sim.shared units:0 units:1
wait seconds 3
quit
